1
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Welcome to Australia!

2
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Australia is a adventure, romance, drama film directed by Baz Luhrmann.

3
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Set in northern Australia before World War II, an English aristocrat who inherits a sprawling ranch
reluctantly pacts with a stock-man in order to protect her new property from a takeover plot.

4
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
As the pair drive 2,000 head of cattle over unforgiving landscape, they
experience the bombing of Darwin by Japanese forces firsthand.

5
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Lady Sarah Ashley, played by Nicole Kidman.

6
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
The Drover, played by Hugh Jackman.

7
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Katherine, played by Essie Davis.

8
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Neil Fletcher, played by David Wenham.

9
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
King Carney, played by Bryan Brown.

10
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
King George, played by David Gulpilil.

11
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Australia is a 2008 epic adventure drama film directed by Baz
Luhrmann and starring Nicole Kidman and Hugh Jackman.

12
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
The screenplay was written by Luhrmann and screenwriter Stuart
Beattie, with Ronald Harwood and Richard Flanagan.

13
01:47:15,000 --> 01:47:21,000
The film is a character story, set between 1939 and 1942 against a dramatised backdrop of events across northern Australia at the time, such as
the bombing of Darwin during World War II, and government policies of seizing half-caste Aboriginal children then in effect.

14
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
Production took place in Sydney, Darwin, Kununurra and Bowen.

15
02:03:45,000 --> 02:03:51,000
The film was released in cinemas on 26 November 2008 in Australia and the United States and on 26 December 2008 in the United Kingdom,
with subsequent worldwide release dates throughout late December 2008, and January and February 2009, by 20th Century Fox.

16
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:06,000
Australia received mixed reviews from critics and
grossed $211 million worldwide.

17
02:20:15,000 --> 02:20:21,000
On 26 November 2023, Faraway Downs, an extended version of the film presented in the form of a six-episode
mini-series, debuted on Disney+ in Australia, Disney+ Hotstar in India and Hulu in the US.

18
02:28:30,000 --> 02:28:36,000
The film explores themes of australia, missionary,
world war ii, ranch, cattle drive.

19
02:36:45,000 --> 02:36:51,000
The tone is emotional.
